+## Dependencies
+
+Provider-signature unit tests precede the verifier. Migration integration precedes the migration. The migration, signature verifier, and callback probes precede the idempotent service; that service and its boundary probes precede the callback route. The migration and workspace-access probe precede the delivery-read route. All implementation work precedes full verification.
+
+## Parallel execution
+
+The signature unit-test and signature-verifier tasks are independent from the schema path and are marked parallel. All database and request-role tasks are deliberately sequential because they share a migration head or mutable test runtime.
+
+## Cross-check verdict
+
+All four requirements in `spec.md` and every planned component in `plan.md` are covered. The callback's invalid-signature, duplicate, persistence-failure/retry, and cross-workspace failure paths are explicit. No implementation work is orphaned. The only reversible assumption is the temporary source layout documented above; reconcile paths to actual repository conventions before implementation while preserving these predicates.
